# Build outputs.
_novo/

# The generated API page.  `novo doc` writes it here, so a reader can
# see what the registry will serve.  The registry gets its own copy,
# uploaded beside the archive by `novo pkg publish`.  The page is
# generated from the sources, so committing it would be committing a
# second original.
APIDOC.md

# The built package binary.  `novo pkg build` names it after the
# package.  A library builds none, so the line is here for when this
# package grows a `main`.
/libicu-sys

# Not novo.lock.  A locked build resolves the same closure twice and
# does it offline once the cache is warm.  A consumer never reads a
# dependency's lock, because it resolves its own closure and writes its
# own.  Committing the lock therefore costs nobody anything and makes
# this repository's builds reproducible.  It is not on the publish
# allow-list, so it never ships either way.
